; ==============================================================================
; Lin Standard Library: Canonical Driver Selftest Corpus
; ==============================================================================
; The single, cross-driver correctness contract every Lin reduction driver must
; satisfy (cpu base engine, SIMD, GPU, and any future driver).
;
; Loading + running this module as a PROGRAM reduces a fixed set of pure probes
; and emits one readback line per probe plus a trailing fold count:
;
;       => <probe-1 value>
;       => <probe-2 value>
;       ...
;       => <folds>            ; native-fold accounting (informational)
;
; The corpus itself is driver-agnostic: it activates NO driver.  The driver
; under test is selected by the *runner* (test/driver_selftest.sh), which wraps
; this file so a driver's std module loads first.  The SAME corpus therefore
; runs unchanged against the base CPU engine (the golden oracle) and against
; every driver; the runner diffs the probe lines.  Because the base engine is
; always the correctness oracle (DESIGN.md), a driver passes the value contract
; iff it reproduces the golden readback values exactly, value-for-value.
;
; The probe values come from core confluence (beta / annihilate / commute /
; erase) plus the one shared scalar-op table (std/drivers/arith.so), so the
; corpus is meaningful under cpu, SIMD and GPU alike and under any future
; driver.  Probes are grouped (see the dividers below) by the redex / capability
; class they stress, so they map onto a driver's claimed LinDriver.caps bits
; (src/lin.h):
;
;   - native small-integer arithmetic  (LIN_CAP_NATIVE_NUM; SIMD claims this)
;     > saturated _op folds: (add 20 22), (div 42 6), ...
;   - comparison / branch folding      (LIN_CAP_NATIVE_NUM)
;     > saturated comparisons fold to Church bools: (leq 3 5), ...
;   - float arithmetic                 (LIN_CAP_NATIVE_NUM)
;     > ffloor (fsqrt 144.0), feq, composed fmul/fadd ...
;   - fixed allocations                (LIN_CAP_FIXED; GPU claims this)
;     > beta-heavy nesting: ((add 20) 22), erasure: ((\x x) 42)
;     > annihilate/erase identity: (fst (pair 7 8)), (second (list3 10 20 30))
;
; Fold accounting: the trailing (folds) line reports how many native folds a
; run performed (base engine cpu folds saturated _op via arith.so too).  This
; is informational and NOT part of the equality contract: folding is each
; driver's own optimization decision, not a requirement (folded need not be
; true).  The runner reports it so a driver that silently stops folding is
; visible, while still failing the run if and only if a value mismatches.
; ==============================================================================

(load "std.lin")

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Group 1 — saturated pure-Lin integer _op folds (LIN_CAP_NATIVE_NUM)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(add 20 22)
(mul 6 7)
(sub 42 42)
(div 42 6)
(mod 17 5)
(pow 2 8)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Group 2 — saturated comparisons fold to Church bools (LIN_CAP_NATIVE_NUM)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(eq 4 4)
(leq 3 5)
(lt 5 3)
(gt 7 3)
(geq 7 7)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Group 3 — composed / deferred operands (fold routing must stay exact)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(mul 6 (add 24 96))
(if (geq 1 (min 4 5)) 1 8)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Group 4 — structure: annihilate / erase identity (LIN_CAP_FIXED)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(fst (pair 7 8))
(snd (pair 7 8))
(second (list3 10 20 30))
((\x x) 42)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Group 5 — float arithmetic folds (LIN_CAP_NATIVE_NUM); _ffi closures
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(ffloor (fsqrt 144.0))
(feq (fadd 2.5 3.5) 6.0)
(ffloor (fmul (fsqrt 16.0) (fadd 1.0 1.0)))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Group 6 — beta-heavy nested currying + arithmetic composition
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
((add 20) 22)
((mul 6) 7)
(mul (add 20 22) 2)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Trailing fold accounting (informational; NOT part of the equality contract)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(folds)